# Copy to .env.order-desk-small, .env.order-desk-medium and .env.order-desk-large, one copy for each runtime, next to docker-compose.order-desk.yml, in /srv/agents/order-desk (RUNBOOK-order-desk.md, "The env files"). Each copy has mode 600 on the host.
# One example serves the three runtimes. Each copy holds the lines of one runtime, and no other line: the shared lines are in .env.order-desk, which the runtime reads first. No name stands in both files.
# Each runtime has a key of its own, and a wallet, an advert and a port of its own. The wallet lock lives in the memory of one process, so two runtimes with one key can spend the same outputs. The compose file gives each runtime its own file.
# The copies hold a key, and they never enter git: the .gitignore of the repository covers .env.* except *.example. Names only here: this example holds no key and no value.
# The supplier key of this runtime. The runtime signs its receipts with it. The service never reads this file. It holds the public values only, in the SMALL_SUPPLIER_PKH, MEDIUM_SUPPLIER_PKH and LARGE_SUPPLIER_PKH lines of .env.order-desk (and the matching public key lines).
# Make the key on the host and write the four values with commands that print nothing. Each runtime gets a different key, and none of them is the key of the service. The four lines are empty here on purpose.
# SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX is the public key, 64 hex characters, and SUPPLIER_PKH is its hash, 56 hex characters. SUPPLIER_ADDRESS is the address of the key, and the wallet of this runtime sits there.
SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PKH=
SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# The advert of this runtime: <transaction hash>#<output index>. The operator posts the three adverts with the hosted tools after the service runs, and writes the reference of each advert here. Each runtime needs its own advert:
# the small runtime the advert of the model lot-small, the medium runtime lot-medium, and the large runtime lot-large. The runtime does not start without this line.
ADVERT_REF=
# The identifier of the agent record: 64 hex characters. All three runtimes name the same record, which lists the three supplier keys. It is the part of AGENT_DID after did:vector:, and it is empty until the record exists.
AGENT_ID=
